extraction_notes: |
  - Dragons and Gods printed 33 (introduction and stat block through Natural Abilities) and
    34 (Ice Breath through Allies; the Rifts block is omitted as on chiang-ku-dragon).
    Printed 50 makes a hatchling of most species an optional player character, says to start
    with no possessions and to use the dragon experience table. Every number was read off a
    render of printed 33 and 34: the text layer carries the digit cipher throughout this
    entry ("306+3" for 3D6+3, "206x l 0" for 2D6x10, "1 04x l 00" for 1D4x100).
  - Shape: chiang-ku-dragon''s, which the sibling batch (kukulcan-dragon, lo-dox-dragon,
    night-stalker-dragon) also follows - a hatchling and an adult variant, each carrying
    attribute dice, pools, horror factor and bonuses (attacks_base included). The top-level
    skills, magic and psionics are the hatchling''s, because printed 50 makes only the
    hatchling a player character and a variant cannot override magic or psionics; the
    adult''s psionics and magic are special abilities. The adult variant''s skill_overrides
    restate the percentages the adult prints. starting_money 0 and equipment_starting []
    are printed 50''s "start with no possessions".
  - xp_table: the Dragon Exp. Table, printed 17, read off a render; the same ladder RUE''s
    dragon-hatchling stores. The table runs to level 30; the app stores 15.
  - Attributes (hatchling) as printed; Spd 6D6 is running, flying 2D6x10 is prose.
  - Hit points 1D4x100, S.D.C. 4D6x10 plus 3D6 per level, P.P.E. 2D4x10 plus 10 per level,
    Horror Factor 10. sdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line.
  - Bonuses are in addition to attribute bonuses. "+2 on all other saving throws" is written
    out across the fourteen d20 saves, as on the Gargoyle Lord; coma_death_pct is left out.
  - Attacks: four physical, attacks_base 4. No hand to hand skill is granted, the related
    picks exclude hand to hand combat skills, and no style is sold (costs {}).
  - Skills: language and basic math at 96%; domestic skills, advanced math and everything
    else at first level proficiency, which is catalog base plus the printed bonus. "Faerie
    lore (10%)" is printed without the plus sign the neighbouring bonuses carry and is read
    as +10% (judgement; a flat 10% would sit below the catalog base). Sculpting & whittling
    (ice) is the catalog Whittling & Sculpting. Dragonese is granted spoken and written;
    the three literacies are Literacy: Other; the spoken languages are eight Language: Other
    picks, the three it reads plus the five additional (judgement). The 12 selections are
    occ_related_skills; Scholar/Technical is Technical. Science is not among them.
  - Psionics: minor, six powers "from either the sensitive or physical categories", read as
    a pick from both; two more at levels 3, 7 and 12. I.S.P. 1D6x10 plus M.E.
  - Magic: the hatchling knows no spells (spells_starting 0). "By 2nd level ... 3D4+3 spells
    from levels 1-3" describes learning, not a grant, and is prose. The adult and
    NPC-hatchling spell lists and the second-discipline table are a special ability.
  - The language and literacy picks carry the printed percentage as a bonus over the
    catalog''s Other rows (Language: Other 50%, Literacy: Other 30%), so each pick starts at
    the printed figure and still climbs; regression refuses a language pick frozen by base.
  - The adult: attacks_base on the adult variant from its printed attacks per melee - seven physical, or four ice breath and three physical, or two by magic.
    Its "+N on all other saving throws" is written out the same way.
  - Natural A.R. is prose (no key); horror_factor is stated on each variant.
---

## Lore

The Ice Dragon may be any shade of blue, light to dark, with white highlights. Ice Dragons once held great power in the Palladium World and commanded large tribes of Orcs, Goblins and Wolfen. The Wolfen once worshipped them and still hold them in the greatest respect, and the feeling is mutual: Ice Dragons are especially fond of the Wolfen (nobody likes Coyles) and often aid the clans in war and espionage. Several serve as honored advisors to Wolfen kings and clan chiefs and are loyal to them - which makes humans and their allies their enemies.

A hatchling is powerful by human standards but only a fraction of the adult it will become: naive, brash, emotional and curious, roughly the equivalent of a young child in understanding of the world.

**Alignment:** Any.

**Size (adult):** 20 to 30 feet (6 to 9 m) tall, up to 65 feet (20 m) long.

**Weight (adult):** 22 tons.

**Habitat:** Anywhere, but prefers moderate to cold climates and loves snow covered tundra, mountains and glaciers - the Old Kingdom, Phi, Lopan, the Eastern Territory, Bizantium and the Great Northern Wilderness. Over 200 are said to live in the Land of the Damned.

**Average Life Span:** 6000 years; some have lived as long as 9000.

**Enemies:** None per se.

**Allies:** An affinity for Algor and other giants, and especially the Wolfen, who welcome Ice Dragons as advisors, friends, allies and honored guests.

## GM Notes

Average experience level of an adult is 1D6+6. The adult variant carries the adult''s attributes (Spd 2D4x10 running, 3D6x10+60 flying), pools, horror factor and bonuses; its psionics and magic are special abilities.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ice-dragon');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ice-dragon';

